    "updated_at": "2018-08-15T21:15:43Z",
    "body": "> WebKit/Chromium/EdgeHTML have 0.75em left/right padding and\r\n> 0.625em bottom padding. Gecko has it the other way around.\r\n\r\nFun historical note:\r\n - Gecko got its current behavior in 2004, to match IE at the time.\r\n - WebKit had the Gecko's prior behavior (matching what Gecko did before that ^ change) up until 2005, at which point they switched to a 3-value padding syntax that was almost but not quite what IE/Firefox had -- they had the last 2 values swapped.\r\n - And now that (mistaken?) WebKit tweak seems to have become the standard. :)\r\n\r\nSee https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1483527#c4 and https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1483527#c5 for links/references",
